  "notes": [
    "psumtree = inline Fenwick BIT with binary-lifting prefix-search; both `set` and `search` are O(log n).",
    "Each step does (i+1) point updates in psumtree (1 for the new vertex + on the order of (agebins) demotions during the age sweep + edges_per_node updates to refresh cited vertices to bucket 0), plus edges_per_node O(log n) searches.",
    "Total cost is O(n * (eps + agebins) * log n) for the random walk + O(n*eps) for the batched edge insert. Edge insert uses `Graph::add_edges` (one rebuild_indexes call) — never per-call `add_edge` (O(m^2) trap).",
    "Compared to ALGO-GN-017 cited_type (linear cumsum per draw), psumtree is significantly faster at large n. cited_type/size_scaling/n_uniform/5000 was ~5.8ms vs lastcit/size_scaling/eps3_decay/5000 at 1.6ms (3.6x faster) despite lastcit's extra age-sweep work — the O(log n) prefix-search dominates as n grows.",
    "agebins_count benchmark shows mild slowdown (152µs → 188µs, ~25%) going from 1 to 16 bins at n=1000, confirming age sweep is a secondary cost compared to the per-edge draw."
  ],
